# Sourced by start-sway(1) under `set -o allexport`, after /etc/sway/environment
# and after the environment.d(5) generator. Plain assignments are therefore
# exported into sway's own environment and inherited by everything sway starts.
#
# Keep driver/compositor variables (SWAY_EXTRA_ARGS, WLR_*) in
# /etc/sway/environment, which is image-level -- sway will not start on this GPU
# without them, so they belong to the artifact rather than to a user.

# Qt has no theming of its own here. Qt selects a platform theme from
# XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, which is "sway", so it matches nothing and falls back to
# a light palette no matter what GTK and the portal are doing. Measured with an
# unset variable: Window #efefef, text #000000, colorScheme Unknown.
#
# "xdgdesktopportal" makes Qt read org.freedesktop.appearance color-scheme from
# the XDG portal -- the same signal GTK4/libadwaita, Firefox, Chromium and
# Electron already follow, so there is one source of truth for the whole
# desktop rather than a parallel Qt-only setting.
#
# Measured against the obvious alternative, QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=gtk3:
#
#                      Window    Base (text fields, lists)
#   gtk3               #323232   #323232   <- identical, fields do not contrast
#   xdgdesktopportal   #323232   #242424   <- distinct, and #242424 is exactly
#                                             the desktop grey in 20-appearance.conf
#
# Both give colorScheme=Dark; gtk3 flattens Base onto Window, which makes text
# inputs and list views disappear into the dialog. Hence the portal one.
#
# Survives boot 2: libqxdgdesktopportal.so ships in qt6-qtbase-gui, which the
# --no-autoremove in build_files/30-kde-remove.sh deliberately keeps, and that
# script's guard rails already assert xdg-desktop-portal{,-gtk} survive.
# KDEPlasmaPlatformTheme6.so would NOT survive -- plasma-integration is on the
# removal list.
QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=xdgdesktopportal
